// Tekken 3 (SLUS_004.02, USA) recompiler seeds.
//
// The emitter already roots the resident program at the PS-X EXE entry, scans executable pointer
// tables, and follows direct calls. Add only entries that those mechanisms cannot discover. A guessed
// address can split a real function and silently corrupt the substrate.
{
  "main": [],

  // FUN_800862D8 writes the interrupt-exit context consumed by BIOS B0:0x19 HookEntryInt. The
  // context's resume word is the instruction after the call, 0x80085DEC; T3-04/C014 verifies that
  // saving call and return edge on retail bytes. The first bounded whole-product run then delivered
  // IRQ 0x004 and read 0x80085DC4 from the game's custom-exit slot at 0x80099BD8. Both are genuine
  // mid-body interrupt re-entry points, not ordinary function seeds. The run failed fast at the
  // absent 0x80085DC4 entry before executing it; no later boundary is inferred.
  "main_reentry": ["0x80085DC4", "0x80085DEC"],

